Regenerate with: git diff --abbrev=7 archive/pre-reset-2026-10-10 -- src/lib/store/posthog-server.ts (keep this header above it).

D048 (task 1.3, QA review N4): import SITE_ENV and stamp `env: SITE_ENV` on `purchase_confirmed` on every non-production
  build, so a test sale on beta, a preview or a local run can never read as revenue. Production's payload is the tag's.
D074 (founder sign-off, chat 26 Nov 2026; K-124; wiki/decisions/D074-refund-event.md): the server also reports a refund.
  New `PURCHASE_REFUNDED = "purchase_refunded"`, the pure `purchaseRefundedEvent(order, refund)` and
  `reportRefundToPostHog(order, refund)`, beside the purchase ones. The send itself (client options, the awaited flush, the
  never-throw "sent" | "skipped" | "failed" contract, the log lines) moves into one private `sendToPostHog`, which
  `reportPurchaseToPostHog` now calls with the same event, the same options and the same log lines; the refund report is
  the second caller, so the flush cannot be forgotten in one of two copies. A refund of no money sends nothing.
  `purchase_refunded` carries transaction_id (the order reference, the join key), currency "INR", value (rupees of this
  refund), tier, partial, source "webhook", the order's campaign keys flat, `$process_person_profile: false` and, off
  production, `env`. Its distinctId is the order's ph_distinct_id, else the order reference, as `purchase_confirmed`'s.
  No name, phone, email, address, child age, payment id or refund id; nothing goes to Meta, GA4 or OpenAI.

D075 (founder's choice, chat 26 Nov 2026; K-124 part b; wiki/decisions/D075-session-id-on-orders.md): `purchaseConfirmedEvent`
adds `$session_id: order.ph_session_id` to the properties, and ONLY when the order stored one (an absent key, never an empty
one), so PostHog attributes the sale to that session's own entry referrer, landing path, click ids and UTMs. Nothing else in
the payload changes; `purchase_refunded` does NOT carry it (a refund days later would stretch the sale's session). The
session id is the same class of random, pseudonymous id as the `ph_distinct_id` already used; no name, phone, email, address
or child detail, and nothing goes to Meta, GA4 or OpenAI.

